<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- SCRUM-91 point of no return: the written mandate PROJECTION is dropped. MSR, its
         only writer, is deleted in this wave; mnd_ext_status (004), mandate_effective_status
         (005) and mandate_current_status (007) derive the state the table used to hold, and
         every other attribute it carried already lives on the MRR request spine.

         WHY THIS FILE AND NOT THE 000 SHARED-CORE BOOTSTRAP. The nine sibling M-services
         carry the identical guarded drop in their own 000-man-core-bootstrap.xml, because a
         shared-core create must not outlive the shape it mints. MRG cannot: its own
         003-man-ext-status-view builds man_ext_status with "FROM mandate", so a drop ordered
         at 000 kills the migration on any fresh database with

             Migration failed for changeset db/changelog/2026/07/003-man-reporting.xml
             relation "mandate" does not exist

         (observed 2026-07-26 on the mrg Testcontainers suite). 003 is applied AND runOnChange,
         so guarding it would re-create the very view 006 drops. The drop therefore lands here,
         last in MRG's master, after 003 has built man_ext_status and 006 has dropped it again.

         NUMBERING: 007 and 008 are taken (007-man-current-status, 008-man-status-history), so
         009 is the next free ordinal, and it must sort last for the reason above.

         NOTHING DEPENDS ON THE TABLE AT DROP TIME. man_ext_status, the only view that ever
         read it, is dropped by 006. mnd_ext_status, mandate_effective_status,
         mandate_current_status and man_ctv_view read the leg reply tables, the MRR spine and
         mandate_override only, so CockroachDB has no view dependency to refuse.

         mandate_reason_code is NOT touched: it is reference data, not projection state. The
         guard makes every reachable database state converge, so a re-run MARK_RANs. -->

    <changeSet id="009-drop-mandate-projection" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN"><tableExists tableName="mandate"/></preConditions>
        <dropTable tableName="mandate"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
